From: erosqcfw <erosqcfw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] output: an explicit enable resets the reopen back-off

After an output fails, LockUpdate() only reopens it once REOPEN_AFTER
(10 s) has passed, unless forced, and MultipleOutputs::Play() never
forces.  Enabling the output again does not touch fail_timer.  On EROS Q
the UI moves playback to the Bluetooth output when Bluetooth headphones
connect; a reconnect within 10 s of the previous disconnect (whose write
failed with ENODEV) left MPD with the Bluetooth output skipped and the
DAC disabled, so it paused with "Failed to open audio output" (HITL
10-21, 6 of 6 failures had a < 10 s gap).  Treat a client's enable as
"try it now".

---
--- a/src/output/Control.cxx	2026-10-21 09:35:52.063422138 +0000
+++ b/src/output/Control.cxx	2026-10-21 09:35:52.073923977 +0000
@@ -131,6 +131,14 @@
 	if (new_value == enabled)
 		return false;
 
+	/* erosq: an explicit enable means "use this output now".  Without
+	   this, an output that failed less than REOPEN_AFTER ago (a
+	   Bluetooth sink that just disconnected) is skipped by the next
+	   non-forced Update(), and with the other output disabled playback
+	   pauses with "Failed to open audio output". */
+	if (new_value)
+		fail_timer.Reset();
+
 	enabled = new_value;
 	return true;
 }
